  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "The auca was present in some other parts of Spain, even though it was most popular in Catalonia. It has a structure somewhat similar to comics, but has more rigid.  The auca has a number of images that can be evenly divided by 4 (usually 48), all images are of the same size, all fit on one page, and there is a small piece of text, called rodolí (pronounced [ruðuˈli], plural rodolins) - underneath every image, usually in the Catalan language and since the 19th century also rhymed."
  },
